            <div xml:id="d260-a1">

                <pb facs="0442" n="340" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg340"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">note verbale</hi>.</head>
                <p>The acting secretary of state of the imperial ministry of foreign affairs
                    acknowledges the receipt of the American ambassador’s note communicating the
                    sorrow of the President and Secretary of State of the United States at the death
                    of the imperial ambassador, Baron Speck von Sternberg. He begs to express to
                    President Roosevelt and to his excellency, Mr. Elihu Root, the thanks of the
                    Imperial Government for the warm sympathy evidenced. The imperial service has
                    suffered a severe loss in the premature passing away of the ambassador at
                    Washington, who was one of its most efficient members.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-08-26"><hi rendition="#italic">August 26,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Foreign Office.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
